+### Relay preflight & wedge watchdog (F295 Half 2)
+
+When a grok worker is created and the resolved model routes through a relay
+(`base_url` in `~/.grok/config.toml`), CAO probes the relay first. If the
+relay is unreachable, creation fails with a structured error naming the
+endpoint and failure kind — no terminal row or tmux window is left behind.
+Knobs: `[grok_cli] relay_preflight` (bool, default true),
+`relay_preflight_timeout_s` (int, default 20) in `providers.toml`.
+
+A live grok worker in PROCESSING for longer than `grok_wedge_age_s` (default
+900, clamped 300-7200) triggers a one-shot inbox notice naming `peek_terminal`
+and `delete_terminal` as the remedy. No automatic action is taken. Knobs:
+`supervisor.watchdog.grok_wedge` (bool), `supervisor.watchdog.grok_wedge_age_s`
+(int) in `settings.json`.
